# gujiconform -- Platform slice 2 (write IO): $h.write on a READ handle is a
# RUNTIME error (Section 15.4 misuse model), identical in both engines. `stdin`
# is a read-only Handle, so writing to it aborts after flushing stdout. The
# pre-error line is on stdout; the process exits non-zero. Engine error text on
# stderr differs, so stderr is not pinned. Derived from the spec, not captured.
sub main(): Int {
    print("before")
    stdin.write("x")
    print("unreachable")
    0
}
